Dave The Diver Save Editor — Attribution & Notices
===================================================

This project is an independent, native macOS (Apple Silicon) save editor for
the game "Dave the Diver". It is a clean Swift reimplementation, not a code
fork, but it stands on the shoulders of prior work and credits it gratefully.

Inspiration & prior art
-----------------------
* DaveSaveEd — https://github.com/FNGarvin/DaveSaveEd (MIT), by FNGarvin.
  The original Windows save editor: the feature set (max Gold/Bei/Artisan's
  Flame/Follower count and ingredients), the ingredient/items reference data,
  and the macOS/Windows save-path knowledge are derived from or inspired by
  this project. Thank you.

* Dave the Diver save-format reverse-engineering — WhiteMinds
  https://github.com/WhiteMinds/dave-diver-expansion (tools/save-codec).
  The correct char-level (UTF-16 code unit) XOR codec understanding — which
  lets this editor handle non-ASCII (Chinese/Korean) saves without corruption,
  unlike byte-level implementations — is based on WhiteMinds' PORTING-NOTES.
  Thank you.

Non-affiliation
---------------
This project and its authors are NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or
associated with Mintrocket, Nexon, or any entity related to "Dave the Diver".
This is an independent, fan-made tool. Use at your own risk; always keep
backups of your save files.

Third-party components
----------------------
* SQLite — public domain. On macOS the system libsqlite3 is linked via the
  SDK's `import SQLite3` module; no SQLite source is vendored in this repo.
